{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01WhST7THBvVmABBTixkUqFr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me verify each acceptance criterion:\n\n**AC1: cmd/du/du_test.go compiles without errors via \"go vet ./cmd/du/...\"** — Verified above, `go vet` passed clean.\n\n**AC2: All test functions use testutils.RunDiffTests** — Every test function calls `testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBinaryPath, refBinaryPath, nil, tests)`. No custom comparison logic.\n\n**AC3: TestMain builds the Go du binary and locates gdu, skipping with os.Exit(0) when gdu not found** — TestMain uses `exec.LookPath(\"gdu\")` and exits 0 if not found, exactly matching the cat/wc pattern.\n\n**AC4: Tests cover all short and long flag forms** — Let me verify the flag coverage:\n\n| Flag | Test function | Test name |\n|------|--------------|-----------|\n| `-a` / `--all` | `TestDU_AllFilesFlag` | `flag_a_all_files`, `long_flag_all` |\n| `-s` / `--summarize` | `TestDU_SummarizeFlag` | `flag_s_summarize`, `long_flag_summarize` |\n| `-c` / `--total` | `TestDU_TotalFlag` | `flag_c_total_single_arg`, `long_flag_total_multiple_args` |\n| `-h` / `--human-readable` | `TestDU_SizeModeFlags` | `flag_h_human_readable_binary`, `long_flag_human_readable` |\n| `--si` | `TestDU_SizeModeFlags` | `flag_si_human_readable` |\n| `-k` | `TestDU_SizeModeFlags` | `flag_k_kilobyte_blocks` |\n| `-m` | `TestDU_SizeModeFlags` | `flag_m_megabyte_blocks` |\n| `-b` / `--apparent-size` | `TestDU_SizeModeFlags` | `flag_b_apparent_size`, `long_flag_apparent_size` |\n| `-L` / `--dereference` | `TestDU_SymlinkHandling` | `flag_L_dereference_symlinks`, `long_flag_dereference` |\n| `-P` | `TestDU_SymlinkHandling` | `flag_P_no_dereference_explicit` |\n| `-0` / `--null` | `TestDU_NullTerminator` | `flag_0_null_terminated`, `long_flag_null` |\n| `-d N` / `--max-depth=N` | `TestDU_MaxDepthFlag` | `flag_d_0_depth_zero`, `flag_d_1_depth_one`, `long_flag_max_depth_1`, etc. |\n| `--block-size=N` | `TestDU_SizeModeFlags` | `flag_block_size_512`, `flag_block_size_4096` |\n| `--` | `TestDU_FlagTerminator` | `double_dash_flag_like_filename`, `double_dash_with_directory` |\n\nAll covered.\n\n**AC5: At least one test exercises hard-link deduplication with os.Link** — `TestDU_HardLinkDeduplication` creates a file, hard-links it via `os.Link`, and verifies both binaries count it once.\n\n**AC6: Test functions organized by PRD requirement section (R1, R2, R3, R4) with section-header comments** — Four section headers present:\n- `R1: Default recursive disk usage behavior (prd009-du R1)`\n- `R2: Size mode and output format flags (prd009-du R2)`\n- `R3: Traversal behavior (prd009-du R3)`\n- `R4: Error handling and exit codes (prd009-du R4)`\n\nAll matching the separator pattern from `cmd/cat/cat_test.go`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":244,"cache_read_input_tokens":62728,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":244},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eb91553c-19d7-4761-90d2-f7b5f9377860","uuid":"db0b6ace-52be-44ba-9310-52d11126a314"}
